NAME
    gcloud run worker-pools logs - read logs for Cloud Run worker pools

SYNOPSIS
    gcloud run worker-pools logs COMMAND [--region=REGION]
        [GCLOUD_WIDE_FLAG ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Read logs for Cloud Run worker pools.

EXAMPLES
    To tail logs for a worker pool, run:

        $ gcloud run worker-pools logs tail my-worker-pool

    To read logs for a worker pool, run:

        $ gcloud run worker-pools logs read my-worker-pool

FLAGS
     --region=REGION
        Region in which the resource can be found. Alternatively, set the
        property [run/region].

GCLOUD WIDE FLAGS
    These flags are available to all commands: --help.

    Run $ gcloud help for details.

COMMANDS
    COMMAND is one of the following:

     read
        Read logs for a Cloud Run worker pool.

     tail
        Tail logs for a Cloud Run worker pool.

NOTES
    These variants are also available:

        $ gcloud alpha run worker-pools logs

        $ gcloud beta run worker-pools logs

